  "description": "This course is dedicated to the comprehensive study of the critical primer authored by Al-Shurunbulālī, a prominent figure in the Hanafi school of thought. His work is celebrated globally as a foundational text for beginners seeking to understand jurisprudence within the Hanafi madhhab.By the conclusion of the course, students will have gained a robust understanding of the Hanafi jurisprudential framework as articulated by Al-Shurunbulālī. They will be equipped with the foundational knowledge necessary to engage with more advanced texts and concepts in Islamic law, fostering their growth as informed scholars and practitioners. Invitation to Learn We invite passionate learners to join us on this enlightening academic journey. As you engage with this critical primer, you will not only enhance your understanding of Hanafi jurisprudence but also develop the analytical skills needed to apply legal principles thoughtfully in various contexts. This course represents a valuable opportunity to immerse yourself in the rich intellectual heritage of the Hanafi school and to contribute meaningfully to the ongoing discourse in Islamic legal studies.",
  "courseIntroduction": "• 1. Foundational Knowledge: The course will introduce students to this esteemed primer, which serves as a gateway to the principles of Hanafi jurisprudence. As a beginner-level book, it lays a solid groundwork for understanding essential legal concepts and methodologies, making it accessible to those new to the study of Islamic law.\n• 2. Unique Perspective on Fiqh: What sets this course apart is its unique approach to fiqh (Islamic jurisprudence). We will delve into the underlying legal principles that shape Hanafi thought, allowing students to grasp the rationale behind various rulings. By contextualizing the material within broader legal frameworks, participants will appreciate the intricacies of Islamic law more profoundly.\n• 3. Introduction to Legal Maxims: A significant component of the course will focus on introducing students to the key legal maxims that govern the derivation of subsidiary matters from established scenarios. These maxims are essential tools for any jurist, as they provide a systematic way to navigate the complexities of legal reasoning and application.\n• 4. Decoding the text: The course will also focus on meticulously decoding the text of the work, providing students with a nuanced understanding of its content. Special attention will be given to scenarios in which later Hanafi jurists expressed differing opinions, enabling participants to explore the richness of scholarly discourse within the tradition. Through in-depth discussions, we will clarify the correct views among these divergent opinions, fostering a deeper appreciation for the intellectual rigor of the Hanafi school. This analytical approach not only enhances students' comprehension of the text but also equips them with critical thinking skills necessary for navigating complex legal issues.\n• 5. Shedding light on basic proofs: The course also illuminates some fundamental basic proofs and evidences commonly utilized within the Hanafi school of thought. We will explore various sources of evidence, including Quranic verses, Hadith, consensus (ijma), and analogy (qiyas), demonstrating how these elements are integrated into the reasoning processes of Hanafi jurists.",
